 also why the volume buttons have  been relocated from the side like on the  ipad pro to the top because that is  where you have the new apple pencil  magnetic charging connector to basically  support the second gen apple pencil and  as you can see it takes up literally the  entire side which is why they move the  volume buttons compared to the ipad pro  where you still have a little bit room  to change the volume and with that said  the new budget ipad 9 is the only ipad  that supports the older apple pencil  which recharges by plugging it into the  lightning port which is also only on the  ipad 9 since the rest of the ipad lineup  has moved on to a usb type-c port and  even better an all-out thunderbolt port  on the ipad pro models which actually  supports hubs that we've used on the m1  mac mini but i guess at least one saving  grace for the budget ipad 9 is that it's  the only one that still features a  headphone jack for those who really care  about that now as far as the speakers  every ipad except for the ipad 9 again  features speakers on both the top and  the bottom which gives you true stereo  sound when in landscape mode while the  ipad pro is actually the only one that  has quad speakers so one two three four  for even better sound and a louder  experience just hear it for yourself  [Music]  so  [Music]  so as you've just heard the ipad 9  doesn't sound as good because the audio  only comes out of one side compared to  both sides on the rest of the ipads and  you probably also noticed that the pros  sound much better and louder especially  on the massive 12.9 inch now moving over  to the front the ipad 9 is the only one  to feature the old square corner display  design compared to nice rounded corners  of even bezels all around on the rest of  the ipad lineup which obviously gives  you a much more immersive experience and  that display on the 12.9 inch model is  absolutely massive and because of that  it's by far the least comfortable to use  as a regular tablet so i honestly think  it's meant to be used with a keyboard  case like apple's magic keyboard  basically creating a laptop replacement  now on the other hand you've got the  ipad mini which is perfect for tablet  use both for kids and adults who just  want to browse the web or play games on  the couch or literally anywhere else and  i'd say that the other three offer a  really good balance between portability  and the option to use like a laptop if  you get a keyboard case like the  logitech combo or folio touch which also  packs a built-in trackpad now as far as  the display quality all of the ipads  except for the budget ipad 9 come with  laminated displays which means that the  display and cover glass are glued  together forming a more solid display  that improves black contrast levels and  doesn't have a visible gap between the  two layers like you get on the ipad 9.  on top of that the ipad 9 is the only  one that doesn't feature an  anti-reflective coating which you might  even be able to tell just from looking  at these two displays and it also  doesn't support dci p3 colors for a more  color accurate display as you see in  this example where it can't show this  specific shade of red as far as the  maximum brightness the ipad pros get  brighter specifically 600 nits when in  regular use compared to 500 on the other  ipads however the 12.9 inch ipad pro is  the only one that features apple's  latest xdr display which uses mini led  technology to get much brighter when  viewing hdr video and movie content all  the way up to 600 nits peak brightness  while also giving you the best and  deepest contrast levels you can get the  only issue is that you can sometimes  notice a blooming or halo glow effect  around bright white sections of the  display especially when the lights are  turned off now on top of all of that the  ipad pros come with the 120hz pro motion  feature which allows the displays to  refresh at up to 120 hertz giving you  much more smooth animations and  scrolling compared to the rest of the  ipads that are stuck at 60 hertz as you  can see in these slow mo clips this  feature alone is the reason why i  personally will never buy an ipad  without 120hz refresh rate especially  since i just upgraded to the iphone 13  pro max which also supports promotion oh  and by the way this feature on the ipad  pros also reduces apple pencil latency  making it feel super smooth and natural  now before i get into the performance i  want to ask you guys to go ahead and  subscribe because we've got a lot more  content coming to you guys including  ipads m1x macbook pros and everything  else so we would really appreciate it  because we're trying to hit a million  before the end of this year so thank you  guys now i do want to mention that the  ipad air is the only one that doesn't  come with the new 12 megapixel ultra  wide selfie camera which gives you a  whole new perspective and it also gives  you center stage support which  automatically keeps your face in the  center of the frame which is really nice  and before the performance there's also  differences in the microphone quality so  here's a quick clip so you can hear it  for yourself this is the microphone  quality on the new 10.2 inch ipad 9.  this is the microphone quality on the  new ipad mini 6. this is the microphone  quality on the 10.9 inch ipad air 4.  this is the microphone quality on the 11  inch m1 ipad pro and finally this is a  microphone quality on the 12.9 inch ipad  pro all right getting into performance  the budget ipad 9 gets the a13 chip the  ipad air gets the a14 the new mini  actually gets the latest a15 which is a  little bit ironic and the ipad pros get  the m1 chip directly from the m1 max as  far as the ram the ipad 9 gets three  gigabytes the mini and the air get four  and the pros actually get a really solid  8 gigabytes of ram with the option of  getting up to 16 gigs if you buy the one  terabyte of storage model which is  insanely expensive now in terms of the  raw cpu performance in geekbench 5  they're all incredibly powerful in terms  of single core performance with the  biggest outlier being the ipad 9. now  this is going to give all of them really  good web browsing performance with the  new ipad mini 6 being surprisingly  almost as fast as the m1 ipad pro  however in the multi-core performance  test you can see where the ipad pro is  getting a massive lead and surprisingly  the mini with the new a15 chip is barely  faster than the a14 in the ipad air now  in terms of raw graphics performance the  ipad 9 starts to fall way behind and  once again the mini is just barely  faster than the air with the ipad pro  gaining an absolutely massive lead so  that brings us to a real world gaming  stress test where the m1 ipad pro pulls  even further ahead but the other ipads  aren't necessarily that bad because even  the budget ipad 9 ran a lot of the most  common games at a perfect and consistent  60 fps at maxed out graphic settings  with no issues including games like call  of duty mobile pokemon unite and league  of legends wild rift it even handled  gangshin impact the most demanding ios  game ever surprisingly well at maxed out  graphics settings but it did suffer from  fps drops that you don't experience on  the other more powerful ipads it was  also not nearly as comfortable as the  other ipads to hold in your hand in game  because of the large top and bottom  bezel which pushes the on-screen  controls further away from the edges of  the ipad making it less comfortable but  by far the most comfortable ipad for  gaming is the new ipad mini because of  the compact size which makes controlling  it very easy and the much lighter weight  making it the most perfect gaming tablet  i have ever used but because of the m1  chip and pro motion display the ipad pro  can actually handle a solid 120 fps in  call of duty mobile as you can see in  this video from golden reviewer and that  is obviously only possible on the ipad  pro models now moving on to some of the  spec differences the budget ipad gets  bluetooth 4.2 compared to 5.0 on the  rest of the ipads and it's the only one  that doesn't support wi-fi six but only  the pros and the new mini have the  option of 5g connectivity now this year  the budget ipad finally comes with 64  gigabytes of base storage making it a  much better value since it matches the  mini and the air but the pros actually  get 128 gigs at the base price which is  definitely a nice upgrade so with all of  that said and compared let's get right  into my purchasing recommendations  starting off with who should be buying  the basic ipad 9. if you don't really  care about having the latest design and  the best display quality then i'd  honestly recommend this budget ipad  because you can obviously get it for  much less than the other models and the  performance is more than good enough for  most people it also has the benefit of  being turned into a decent laptop  replacement thanks to the smart  connector and of course it has the  headphone jack for those who really want  to use it but unfortunately the speakers  aren't that great now if you do care  about getting a more future proof design  that looks more modern with the rounded  quarter display and one that comes with  modern specs and features like the usb  type c port the 2nd gen apple pencil  support and the true stereo speakers in  landscape mode then i would recommend  getting a more expensive ipad like the  ipad mini 6. this one is really meant  for people who already have a laptop or  computer for their productivity work and  they just want a tablet to use on the  couch for tablet things like surfing the  web and using social media and just like  i mentioned before i think this is by  far the best tablet for gaming because  of the compact and lightweight size  combined with the impressive a15 chip  that handles any game out there with  ease it's also by far the best option  for kids again because of the smaller  size now if you want something exactly  like the mini but with a larger more  immersive display then the ipad air is  the next step up and the added benefit  of the smart connector means you can  also use it as a laptop replacement just  keep in mind that for the extra 100  dollars you don't get any extra base  storage and it actually comes with the  older and slightly slower a14 chip and  it doesn't come with features like the  12 megapixel ultra wide selfie camera  and the rear facing flash and i would  honestly steer people away from buying  the ipad air right now because we're  expecting it to get updated in the  springtime next year to add in those  missing features and get updated with  the a15 chip and another huge reason is  that it's only 200 less expensive than  the ipad pro and it lacks a ton of  features including the 120hz display the  quad speakers the 600 nits of brightness  the extra cameras on the back the better  microphones optional 5g connectivity the  thunderbolt port the extra 4 gigabytes  of ram and of course the massive  difference in performance which all  together make it much more future proof  so if you're already spending 600 bucks  on the air the ipad pro is a no-brainer  for 200 more since it also comes with  double the storage space 128 gigs  instead of 64. and that 120 hertz  promotion feature is an absolute game  changer and then of course the 12.9 inch  ipad pro for 1100  is meant for the real professionals out  there who want to use it for work or  professional editing or simply anyone  who really cares about having the best  display out there thanks to the new mini  led tech or maybe you just like the  massive display size so with all that  said let me just make it simple for you  if you want a reliable ipad but don't  want to spend a ton of cash just go for  the budget ipad 9. if you want something  small and compact but very powerful and  reliable for everyday casual use then  buy the new ipad mini but out of all of  these ipads i would honestly recommend  the 11 inch ipad pro because it gives  you by far the best value for everything  you're getting making it the most future  proof for the amount of cash especially  since it's on sale on amazon right now  for 750 dollars so hopefully this video  helped you make a decision and if it did  i'm gonna put links to the best deals on  all of these ipads down in the  description below and be sure to click  that circle above to subscribe for more  helpful videos like this one thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

